> > bu
> > Combines with the previous word to make a Lojban letteral, provided tha=
t it is not one of the quote cmavo (ZO, ZOI, LOhU, LEhU) or one of the eras=
ure cmavo (SI, SA, SU), ZEI, or FAhO. If the aforementioned previous word i=
s already a letteral, the resulting letteral will not necessarily be the sa=
me, for instance, "ky. bu" is different from "ky". In addition to single wo=
rds, bu can be combined with a letteral that is already a composite of a wo=
rd+bu, a zei-lujvo, a zo-quoted word, a lo'u-quoted string of words or a zo=
i-quoted foreign text. If there is no previous word, "bu" is in error; this=
 entails that "bu bu" by itself is also ungrammatical.
> =20
> LEhU shouldn't be there, it's at most a magic word assistant, not a magic=
 word. "le'u bu", "le'u zei valsi", "le'u si" should be fine, unless le'u h=
as already been claimed by lo'u, but that's no different than for any other=
 word. LEhU is like a zoi-delimiter, except LOhU always brings its own assi=
stant whereas ZOI picks one from the members of the public. =20
>  =20
> > ba'e (BAhE)
> > Emphasize next word. Forethought emphasis indicator. Indicates that nex=
t word is especially emphasized or emphatic. For grammatical purposes, "ba'=
e" marks the following word but does not change its nature. (The construct =
behaves just as the marked word by itself.) The two words are considered di=
stinct for "sa" matching purposes. Multiple BAhE cmavo may be used in succe=
ssion, and they combine to mark the next non-BAhE word. =20
> > See also za'e, .ui, sa, "Magic Words".
> > =20
> > Keywords: Emphasize next word, emphasize next.
